# Milanote → Cursor Implementation Workflow

Milanote is the source of truth for task completion. Feature markdown under `.cursor/milanote/` is the implementation brief.

## Milanote authoring

Todo items must use keyword prefixes (indentation is ignored for markdown export; **API sync uses Milanote `parentId`** to nest Feature under Category and tasks under Feature):

- `Category: Name` — opens a category
- `Feature: Name` — opens a feature under the current category
- Other items under a Feature — tasks of that feature (see section tags below)
- Other items under a Category but not a Feature — Category **Bugs** feature
- Other items with no Category — overall **Bugs / Bugs**

Only Milanote todo lists whose title contains **Current Phase** are imported (API and markdown export).

### Section tags (inside a Feature)

- `Requirement:` — `## Requirements`
- `Note:` — `## Notes`
- `AI:` — `## AI Context`
- `Bug: text` — that item is a `## Bugs` entry; only its Milanote child tasks are also Bugs
- `Bugs` / `Bugs:` — Bugs list root (empty body omitted); only child tasks become `## Bugs` entries
- `Review: text` — that item is a `## Review` entry; only its Milanote child tasks are also Review
- `Review` / `Review:` — Review list root; includes itself when named `Review`, plus child tasks only
- Unprefixed items (not under a Bug/Review parent) go to `## Tasks`

Bug/Review membership uses Milanote `parentId` (API sync), not document order — siblings after a Bug/Review item stay Tasks unless they are children of that item.

`## Review` is **developer-only**. The agent must not implement, tick, or rewrite Review items. Treat Review as playtest / verification notes for the human developer.

## Ownership

Importer-owned (regenerated on sync — do not treat as editable source of truth for tasks):

- Title, Category, Status
- Requirements / Tasks / Notes / Bugs / Review / AI Context
- Metadata (Milanote ID, Last Sync)

Cursor-owned (append-only for the agent; preserved across syncs):

- `## Cursor Implementation`
- `## Files Modified`
- `## Testing Instructions`
- `## Cursor Notes`

Developer-owned (never edit):

- `## Developer Verification`
- `## Review` (importer-owned content, developer completes in Milanote / playtest)

## After implementing a feature

1. Update `## Cursor Implementation` — what changed, assumptions, architecture decisions, limitations. Keep it concise.
2. Update `## Files Modified` — list every file touched (paths relative to the project).
3. Update `## Testing Instructions` — numbered, deterministic, observable steps plus expected results.
4. Optionally update `## Cursor Notes` — performance, follow-ups, known gaps for future sessions.

## Hard rules

- Never tick generated task checkboxes or rewrite Milanote task lists to mark work done.
- Never mark Features complete / change Status / move files to `_complete`.
- Never edit `## Developer Verification` or treat `## Review` as agent work.
- Never sync completion back to Milanote; the developer marks Milanote tasks after playtest.
- Prefer reading `.cursor/milanote/CURRENT.md` first for active priorities.

## Playtest loop

```text
Sync Milanote → Cursor implements → Cursor documents → Developer playtests
→ Developer verifies → Developer marks Milanote complete → Sync again
```
